WEBVTT

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.684
Billiard is about, you know,

00:09:31.708 --> 00:09:33.268
this ball has to go in the hole

00:09:33.292 --> 00:09:36.143
and which is the one
that I need to kick for that one to go.

00:09:36.167 --> 00:09:40.351
And that means that you have to be able
to think multiperspective.

00:09:40.375 --> 00:09:43.851
And when I think about power,

00:09:43.875 --> 00:09:46.434
I look at the interdependence of parts

00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:49.393
and on some things, I say,
"Power for what?"

00:09:49.417 --> 00:09:51.518
And is it power to or power over?

00:09:51.542 --> 00:09:53.976
And is it power that actually, you know --

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.684
I'll give you one of the --
I'm switching mid-sentence.

00:09:57.708 --> 00:09:59.476
AG: You're also dodging my question.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.351
EP: No, no, because listen to this,